  "content": "Information theory studies the quantification, storage, and communication of information. Shannon entropy measures the average uncertainty in a random variable. Channel capacity is the highest rate at which information can be sent over a noisy channel with vanishing error probability.\n\nIn molecular communication, DNA-based encoding uses nucleotide sequences as the physical medium that carries messages through a fluid channel. Ergodic mixing in that channel is often assumed so that time averages equal ensemble averages. The decoder then treats successive observations as independent draws from a stationary distribution.",
